<title>BRAZIL: Brazil sets up $200 mln farmers credit line.</title>
<headline>Brazil sets up $200 mln farmers credit line.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Monetary Council (CMN) Thursday approved a special 200 million real credit line for farmers to buy tractors and harvesters, said Pedro Parente, executive secretary of the Finance Ministry.</p>
<p>Parente told reporters the credit lines, to be administered by the National Development Bank (BNDES), would pay a fixed 16 percent a year interest and have a five-year maturity.</p>
<p>He said the credit would help cope with a recent increase in demand for tractors and harvesters.</p>
<p>-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358</p>
